readprov_* -- images whose segments declare memory the file does not hold, or
no access at all, for `kuna read --json`'s `provenance` (GH #1401;
decompiler/crates/kuna-cli/tests/read_provenance_cli.rs).

What they are
  readprov_macho_arm64    arm64 Mach-O executable from readprov_macho.s (the
                          issue's fixture plus a __DATA segment):
                            __PAGEZERO 0x0, vmsize 0x100000000, filesize 0, initprot ---
                            __TEXT     0x100000000, 0x4000 of 0x4000 in the file, r-x
                            __DATA     0x100004000, vmsize 0xc000, filesize 0x4000, rw-
                                       (a 0x8000-byte zerofill __bss)
                            __LINKEDIT 0x100010000, vmsize 0x4000, fileoff 0x8000,
                                       filesize 0x2e0, r--
  readprov_elf_x86_64     x86-64 ELF from readprov_elf.S + readprov_elf.ld:
                            PT_LOAD 0x400000, 0xef bytes, R E
                            PT_LOAD 0x401000, 8 bytes at offset 0x1000, no flags
                            PT_LOAD 0x402000, filesz 8, memsz 0x48 (.bss), RW
  readprov_pe_x86_64.exe  x86-64 PE from readprov_pe.S, ImageBase 0x140000000:
                            .data   0x140003000, VirtualSize 0x2008, 0x200 raw at 0x800
                            .sealed 0x140006000, 8 bytes at 0xa00, characteristics
                                    0x08000040 (no MEM_READ, MEM_WRITE or MEM_EXECUTE)

How they were built (no macOS SDK or MSVC; host clang + the rustup-bundled LLD)
  GL=$(rustc --print sysroot)/lib/rustlib/x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu/bin/gcc-ld
  clang -target arm64-apple-macos11 -c readprov_macho.s -o macho.o
  $GL/ld64.lld -arch arm64 -platform_version macos 11.0 11.0 -e _main \
      -o readprov_macho_arm64 macho.o
  python3 readprov_macho_arm64.py readprov_macho_arm64 readprov_macho_arm64
  clang -target x86_64-linux-gnu -c readprov_elf.S -o elf.o
  $GL/ld.lld -static -nostdlib --build-id=none -T readprov_elf.ld \
      -o readprov_elf_x86_64 elf.o
  clang -target x86_64-pc-windows-msvc -c readprov_pe.S -o pe.obj
  $GL/lld-link /brepro /entry:main /subsystem:console /nodefaultlib \
      /dynamicbase:no /fixed /section:.sealed,P /out:readprov_pe_x86_64.exe pe.obj
  Ubuntu clang 14.0.0-1ubuntu1.1, LLD 20.1.8 (rustc 1.90.0). ld64.lld sizes
  __LINKEDIT's memory to its file content; readprov_macho_arm64.py rounds its
  vmsize up to the 16 KiB page the way Apple's ld64 does, which is the layout
  the issue reports (its stale code signature is never read). The output names
  matter: ld64.lld signs with the output file's name.

  sha256:
    df44937763178358cb8f5648b662c06a9c65e0cf9df5843a527d5f3eb5ad9ba9  readprov_macho_arm64
    6d4424266a1fac102b9a216e8b0668775496f8d2cbc5fca32f4b2212904e917f  readprov_elf_x86_64
    a37724af1af1a180c37211e93bb3b5bd9300ff132b3a8af7605f0b32d92e4200  readprov_pe_x86_64.exe
  Never executed. Prebuilt because CI has no Mach-O or PE linker.
